      "text": "Her prayer may seem somewhat selfish, but she was making a promise to God on this behalf in hopes that God was really there for her. It wasn’t about how many kids she could have. That was not what her faith was in. Her faith was in the Lord, and it seemed like the Lord was far from her at the moment. This plea was a prayer of drawing. She wanted to draw closer to the Lord in her faith, and she desired that the Lord would prove that He was not done with her. Prayers for God’s proofs are not sinful or selfish. They can become sinful and selfish, however, when we make a promise to God (like giving our only child over to become a priest and a Nazarite) and then not keeping the promise!",
