          "verse": 1,
          "startVerse": 1,
          "endVerse": 2,
          "author": "Tried By Fire",
          "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
          "text": "There’s quite a story being painted here. It seems that this Elkanah had two wives. Of course, God does not approve of this, and He never did. God records the sins of the people as well as the blessings. This is proven over and over again, including in the life of Abraham who married Hagar as his second wife because he was afraid that God would not keep His promises through his old wife Sarah. Story and context for a different study, no doubt… This is for our learning, and our learning alone. The important note is that one wife could not have kids, while the other wife could.",
          "likes": 0,
          "isLikedByUser": false,
